<title>FRANCE: Valeo head sees euro depressing prices.</title>
<headline>Valeo head sees euro depressing prices.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The head of French car parts manufacturer Valeo, Noel Goutard, said on Wednesday he believed the introduction of a single European currency would have a &quot;profound deflationary effect&quot; on prices.</p>
<p>&quot;When you have prices in euros in Cologne (Germany) and you live in Alsace (France), and you can go and compare prices, the advantages and terms, without racking your brains on the exchange rate between the mark and the franc...I am convinced this will produce a profound deflationary effect, and result in an equalisation of prices towards the lowest common denominator,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
<p>Europe is due to introduce a single currency on January 1, 1999, and though euro notes and coins will not go into full public circulation until 2002, officials are considering calling for prices to be displayed in both national currencies and euros in the interim period.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
